{"kind":"report","text":"U4 step A, at main c8189f7c.\n\nSemantic identifier: kept. Open Counter 0.7.0 (apps/counter/release-identifiers.json) has semantic sha256:a5a44ebc…, which equals signed 0.6.0's (apps/counter/releases/0.6.0). The entry and the definition (b5582434) are unchanged. In-place applies.\n\nPresentation: 0.6.0 905a3f7e, open 0.7.0 9df0d33e.\n\nWhat a user sees change from 0.6.0 to 0.7.0: nothing.\n- Since 0.6.0's signing at 66c70688, apps/counter has changed only in the version string (dap.application.json, package.ts) and the identifiers.\n- The bundle's client changes are application-gateway.ts (U3's matcher, which no longer compares the presentation), application-install.ts and install-request.ts (CLI only). None of them draws anything.\n- The page's title, heading and footer are the same in both versions.\n\nMarker, proposed: one footer line, \"Counter 0.7.0\". `view.ts` takes the version from `apps/counter/dap.application.json` by a JSON import (the browser tsconfig already sets resolveJsonModule), so each later version bump moves it with no second edit. The line is always visible on the installed screen and the demo page, beside the footer buttons. It has `data-release`, so the step B driver reads it without matching layout text. A unit case in app.test.ts checks that the footer shows the manifest's version.\n\nThis is a presentation change, so 0.7.0's open presentation moves from 9df0d33e. The head carries the new identifier and the page and module seals, and it runs the full gate. You sign 0.7.0 from main after it lands. Then the trust-row head follows.\n\nI start the marker head after your deployment END, because no compile runs before it. Unless you object, I build it as proposed.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}